is fair to use the same field to identify the current version of a specific entity. In other
words, the timestamp field, in addition to the ID of that specific entity, would define a
specific version of an entity. Let's utilize the If-None-Match header to check whether
there were any changes made on the given entity since it was loaded by the client
application. First, we will check whether the client has sent the conditional header:
// Get the version stamp of the entity
var entityTag = string.Empty;
if (Request.Headers.ContainsKey("If-None-Match"))
{
entityTag = Request.Headers["If-None-Match"].First();
}
